{
  "id": 1,
  "slug": "first-kite",
  "title": "First Kite",
  "concept": "What makes a subnet public, and how a request reaches an application through a load balancer.",
  "guidance": "full",
  "region": "us-east-1",
  "azs": 2,
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "welcome",
      "text": "Welcome to the sky above N. Virginia. The dashed border is your VPC: your own region of the AWS network. The Cloudlings on the ground are the internet, and their kites are requests. Right now there is no way in.",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "acknowledged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "instances",
      "text": "Two EC2 instances are already running in the mid band, in private subnets. They are locked for now; we will look inside them in the next level. Our job is to let the green kites reach them safely.",
      "highlight": "resource:app-a",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "acknowledged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "place-igw",
      "text": "First, a gate. Drag the Internet Gateway from the tray into the sky.",
      "highlight": "palette:igw",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "resource-exists",
          "resourceId": "igw"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "add-route",
      "text": "A gate is no use without a signpost. Click a public subnet in the low band and add a route: Internet (0.0.0.0/0) to the Internet Gateway. That route is what makes a subnet public.",
      "highlight": "subnet:public-a",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "route-present",
          "routeTableId": "rt-public",
          "destination": "internet",
          "target": "internet-gateway"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "place-alb",
      "text": "Now the front door. Drag the Application Load Balancer into the sky. It will settle across both public subnets, one node in each Availability Zone.",
      "highlight": "palette:alb",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "resource-exists",
          "resourceId": "alb"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "open-sg",
      "text": "The load balancer wears a security group, drawn as a pencilled outline, and it starts with no inbound rules, so everything is refused. Click the load balancer and add an inbound rule: HTTPS 443 from Anywhere.",
      "highlight": "resource:alb",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "security-group-allows",
          "securityGroupId": "sg-alb",
          "ports": "https",
          "peer": {
            "kind": "anywhere"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "listener",
      "text": "The green kites fly on HTTPS 443. On the same card, set the listener to HTTPS 443 so the load balancer is listening on that port.",
      "highlight": "resource:alb",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "listener-is",
          "loadBalancerId": "alb",
          "listener": "https"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "targets",
      "text": "Last, tell the load balancer where to send requests. On its card, tick both EC2 instances as targets (or drag from its handle to each instance).",
      "highlight": "resource:alb",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "scene",
        "predicate": {
          "kind": "targets-registered",
          "loadBalancerId": "alb",
          "atLeast": 2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fly",
      "text": "Ready. Press \"Fly kites\" and watch. Three green kites are visitors; the red one is aiming at SSH 22.",
      "highlight": "button:fly",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "level-complete"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "inspect",
      "text": "Click any Cloudling to see its kite's journey, check by check. The red kite bounced off the outline: no rule allows port 22, and a security group refuses whatever it does not allow.",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "acknowledged"
      }
    }
  ],
